  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/DataDog/datadog-lambda-python/zipball/v8.128.0",
  "body": ">[!IMPORTANT]\r\n> For Python 3.8 and 3.9: `dd-trace-py` version is [v3.19.8](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/releases/tag/v3.19.8)\r\n> For Python >= 3.10: `dd-trace-py` version is [v4.15.2](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-trace-py/releases/tag/v4.12.2)\r\n\r\n\r\n>[!IMPORTANT]\r\n> This layer is currently unavailable in aws region `me-south-1`, due to unrelated incidents\r\n\r\n\r\n## What's Changed\r\n* Delete Github secrets used in update snapshots workflow by @rithikanarayan in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-python/pull/852\r\n* fix: use DD_SERVICE for inferred spans when integration service names are removed by @zarirhamza in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-python/pull/834\r\n* fix(deps): vuln minor: shell-quote · patch: brace-expansion [tests/integration] by @gh-worker-campaigns-3e9aa4[bot] in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-python/pull/850\r\n* chore: raise compressed layer size limit to 10 MB by @joeyzhao2018 in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-python/pull/857\r\n* fix: parent lazily imported module spans to the function span by @joeyzhao2018 in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-python/pull/856\r\n* v8.128.0 by @joeyzhao2018 in https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-python/pull/858\r\n\r\n### Layers\r\n```\r\n# AWS Commercial\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python38:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python38-ARM:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python39:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python39-ARM:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python310:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python310-ARM:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python311:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python311-ARM:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python312:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python312-ARM:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python313:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python313-ARM:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python314:128\r\narn:aws:lambda:<AWS_REGION>:464622532012:layer:Datadog-Python314-ARM:128\r\n\r\n# AWS GovCloud \r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python38:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python38-ARM:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python39:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python39-ARM:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python310:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python310-ARM:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python311:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python311-ARM:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python312:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python312-ARM:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python313:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python313-ARM:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python314:128\r\narn:aws-us-gov:lambda:us-gov-<AWS_REGION>:<ACCOUNT>:layer:Datadog-Python314-ARM:128\r\n\r\nACCOUNT =\r\n002406178527 for us1 environment\r\n486696501492 for us2 environment\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/DataDog/datadog-lambda-python/compare/v8.127.0...v8.128.0\r\n",
